                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of a
            %em premodel category
            is a relaxation of the notion of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} Combinatorial
            premodel categories form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            that has all (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+diagram"}> small
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            and has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representing+objects"} representing objects
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctors"} Quillen bifunctors
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of combinatorial
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            premodel categories is the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules+over+a+monoid"} modules over a monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in this
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+2-category"} model 2-category
            structure. In this model structure, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functor"} left Quillen functor
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            if and only if it is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong premodel category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicomplete+category"} bicomplete category
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi AF
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,AF)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi AC
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (AC,F)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AC
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AC\subset C
            (equivalently,
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi AF
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AF\subset F
          %p
            The members of AC are called
            %strong anodyne cofibrations
            and the members of AF are called
            %strong anodyne fibrations
            (as in
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anodyne+morphism"} anodyne morphism
          %h2#criteria_for_model_categories Criteria for model categories
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} Model categories
            can be singled out among premodel categories by imposing the additional requirement that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi AF
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi AC
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  W
                  \\coloneqq
                  AF \circ AC
                  \\,,
          %p
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AC
            with those of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi AF
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AF
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3+property"} 2-out-of-3 property
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#csElegance"} Cavallo &amp; Sattler 2022, Theorem 3.8
          #CriteriaCases.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              In a premodel category,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              satisfies the 2-out-of-3 property if and only it the following conditions are satisfied:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g,f
                  are cofibrations such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                  are anodyne cofibrations, then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is an anodyne cofibration. If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g,f
                  are fibrations such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  are anodyne fibrations, then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                  is an anodyne fibration.
              %li
                %p
                  Any (cofibration, anodyne fibration) factorization or (anodyne cofibration, fibration) factorization of a map in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is an (anodyne cofibration, anodyne fibration) factorization.
              %li
                %p
                  Any composite of an anodyne fibration followed by an anodyne cofibration is in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %h2#anodyne_and_trivial_cofibrations Anodyne and trivial (co)fibrations
          %p
            The notion of premodel category doesn’t come with a good general notion of weak equivalence. But if a particular premodel category has a good notion of weak equivalence, such as one of
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a{:href => "#Barton"} Barton
            = succeed "," do
              %em relaxed premodel categories
          %ul
            %li
              An
              %strong anodyne cofibration
              is a member of the class AC
            %li
              A
              %strong trivial cofibration
              is a cofibration that is also a weak equivalence
          %p
            In principle one must also distinguish a third class of cofibrations that have the left lifting property with respect to fibrations between fibrant objects. However, in a relaxed premodel category, these are trivial cofibrations. (
            %a{:href => "#Barton"}> Barton, Prop 3.5.2
            )
          %h2#Cylindrical Cylindrical premodel categories
          %p
            A
            %strong cylindrical
            premodel category is one equipped with well-behaved
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder"} cylinder
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocylinder"} cocylinder
            functors. In the following, we assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete"} finitely complete
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+cocomplete"} finitely cocomplete
            category.
          .num_defn
